# Allow the 'ec_su_axb35' group to write the APU power-mode sysfs file.
# The D-Bus service (com.evox2.powermode) runs as the user and writes this file;
# granting group write avoids setuid/polkit for a single-file homelab box.
#
# Caveats (verified on this box, 2026-08-21):
#  - udev rules set permissions on device *nodes* (/dev/...), NOT on sysfs
#    attribute files. The ec_su_axb35 module creates its devices with a
#    character device node but no cdev open handler, so the node is unusable
#    and udev cannot change the mode of apu/power_mode.
#  - udev also warns that a non-system group owning a device node is
#    deprecated, so this rule is kept minimal and only sets the group on the
#    (currently unused) device node.
#
# The real permission grant happens at module load: the module (or a patched
# version, see #3 kernel PR) must call sysfs file permission setup for
# apu/power_mode, e.g. via a udev tag or an explicit set of the file's group
# and mode in the driver's device_create path. Until then, the D-Bus service
# falls back to writing via a sudo rule (see README.md).
SUBSYSTEM=="ec_su_axb35", KERNEL=="apu", GROUP="ec_su_axb35"
